\title{Descent for surjective maps}
\taxon{Module}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\date{2026-09-10}

\import{stt-macros}

\p{
We formalise the descent property of [surjections](Core.SurjectiveMaps).
}

\agda{
module Core.DescentSurjectiveMaps where

open import Axioms.UF
}

\agda-imports{
\agda{
open import Foundations.Prelude
open import Core.Arrows
open import Core.CartesianSquares
open import Core.SurjectiveMaps
}
}

\subtree[stt-00YZ]{
\title{Descent for surjections in terms of cartesian squares}
\taxon{Theorem}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\date{2026-09-10}

\p{
Consider a commuting diagram

\quiver{
\begin{tikzcd}
  \cdot && \cdot && \cdot \\
  \\
  \cdot && \cdot && \cdot
  \arrow[from=1-1, to=1-3]
  \arrow[from=1-3, to=1-5]
  \arrow[from=1-1, to=3-1]
  \arrow[from=1-3, to=3-3]
  \arrow[from=1-5, to=3-5]
  \arrow[from=3-1, to=3-3, two heads]
  \arrow[from=3-3, to=3-5]
  \arrow[from=1-1, to=3-3, phantom, "\lrcorner" very near start]
\end{tikzcd}
}

where the left square is a pullback and where the bottom left horizontal map is
surjective. Then the right square is a pullback if and only if the outer rectangle is
a pullback.
}

\p{This theorem appears as Theorem 2.3 in Cherubini–Rijke \citek{CR21}.}

\proof{
\p{
Assume given the diagram

\quiver{
\begin{tikzcd}
  \cdot && \cdot && \cdot \\
  \\
  X && Y && \cdot
  \arrow[from=1-1, to=1-3]
  \arrow[from=1-3, to=1-5]
  \arrow["f"', from=1-1, to=3-1]
  \arrow["g" description, from=1-3, to=3-3]
  \arrow["h", from=1-5, to=3-5]
  \arrow["i"', from=3-1, to=3-3, two heads]
  \arrow["j"', from=3-3, to=3-5]
  \arrow[from=1-1, to=3-3, phantom, "\lrcorner" very near start]
\end{tikzcd}
}

Since the left square is a pullback, we have a family of equivalences
#{\Pi_{(x : X)}(\fibre{f}{x}\simeq \fibre{g}{i(x)})}. We need to show that
#{\Pi_{(y : Y)}(\fibre{g}{y}\to \fibre{h}{j(y)})} is a family of equivalences if and
only if #{\Pi_{(x : X)}(\fibre{f}{x}\to \fibre{h}{j(i(x))})}, but this is an
[easy corollary](stt-00YW) of the [propositional induction property](stt-00YY) of
surjections.
}
}

\agda{
module _
  {𝓤 𝓥 𝓦 𝓧 𝓨 𝓩}
  {A : Type 𝓤} {B : Type 𝓥} {C : Type 𝓦}
  {X : Type 𝓧} {Y : Type 𝓨} {Z : Type 𝓩}
  {f : A → X} {g : B → Y} {h : C → Z}
  (R : Arrow-map g h) (L : Arrow-map f g)
  (surj : is-surjective (Arrow-map.bot L))
  (cart-L : is-cartesian L)
  where

  descent-is-surjective
    : is-cartesian (paste-squares R L) → is-cartesian R
  descent-is-surjective cart-RL
    = is-fibrewise-equiv←surjective-restrict surj (arrow-fibre R)
        (λ x → 3-for-2~' (arrow-fibre-∘ R L x) (cart-L x) (cart-RL x))

  descent-is-surjective-iff
    : is-cartesian R ↔ is-cartesian (paste-squares R L)
  descent-is-surjective-iff
    = ((λ cart-R → compose-cartesian cart-R cart-L) , descent-is-surjective)
}
}

\subtree[stt-00YX]{
\title{Descent for surjections in terms of pullback cones}
\taxon{Corollary}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\date{2026-09-10}

\p{
Using the [characterisation of cartesian squares by pullback cones](stt-003C),
we obtain the same descent property for the canonical gap maps.
}

\agda{
module _
  {𝓤 𝓥 𝓦 𝓧 𝓨 𝓩}
  {A : Type 𝓤} {B : Type 𝓥} {C : Type 𝓦}
  {X : Type 𝓧} {Y : Type 𝓨} {Z : Type 𝓩}
  {f : A → X} {g : B → Y} {h : C → Z}
  (R : Arrow-map g h) (L : Arrow-map f g)
  (surj : is-surjective (Arrow-map.bot L))
  (pb-L : is-pullback (Cone←Arrow-map L .snd))
  where

  descent-is-surjective-pullback
    : is-pullback (Cone←Arrow-map (paste-squares R L) .snd)
    → is-pullback (Cone←Arrow-map R .snd)
  descent-is-surjective-pullback pb-RL
    = is-pullback←is-cartesian R
        (descent-is-surjective R L surj
          (is-cartesian←is-pullback L pb-L)
          (is-cartesian←is-pullback (paste-squares R L) pb-RL))

  descent-is-surjective-pullback-iff
    : is-pullback (Cone←Arrow-map R .snd)
    ↔ is-pullback (Cone←Arrow-map (paste-squares R L) .snd)
  descent-is-surjective-pullback-iff
    = ( λ pb-R
        → is-pullback←is-cartesian
            (paste-squares R L)
            (compose-cartesian
              (is-cartesian←is-pullback R pb-R)
              (is-cartesian←is-pullback L pb-L)))
    , descent-is-surjective-pullback
}
}
